35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,#### Turn 1 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Kenji,,#### Turn 1 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,#### Turn 1 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"- **Yumi**: The scope freeze was a myth. Two new accounts forced two rewrites, and the plan died within a year.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,- **Benjamin**: The dispatch tool skipped three upgrades since 2012. We let it rot because testing took too long.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,#### Turn 2 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Kenji,,#### Turn 2 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"- **Toshio**: The board trimmed capital for three years, yet operating lines passed without question. We are funding the bleed, not the fix.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"- **Yumi**: @Toshio, that explains the trap. We keep paying for the mess instead of fixing the root cause.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, exactly. The rot is structural. We’ve been patching symptoms while the core decays.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,#### Turn 3 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Kenji,,- **Kenji**: The peak season has no freeze window. One bad cutover means two days of paper dispatch. We can’t afford that.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, that timing risk is real, but the invoices show the real trap. Bundled prices held steady, while separate add-ons climbed yearly. We are buying a leaky bucket.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"- **Yumi**: @Toshio, that leaky bucket is exactly why the scope kept shifting. We can't fix the plan if the budget is already broken.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, the invoices confirm the pattern. We pay for the band-aid, not the surgery. The 2018 data lift proves external work returns broken.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I found two admins retiring this year, and the last posting stayed open eleven months. We are losing the people who actually know how this works.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: The yard scanners are a mess of old models, and the 2021 trial died in spreadsheets. Our hardware can’t support a modern system.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"The invoices confirm it. Bundled deals held steady, but separate add-ons climbed yearly. We are funding the bleed, not the fix.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Toshio"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Toshio: The invoices confirm it. Bundled deals held steady, but separate add-ons climbed yearly. We are funding the bleed, not the fix.""}]}"
53,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"- **Yumi**: And the winter outage sat unowned for two days. Four suppliers, zero accountability. We are walking into that trap again.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, the unowned outage and the broken data lift are the same failure. We outsource the risk, then inherit the repair.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
