60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,#### Turn 1 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Kenji,,- **Kenji**: So we have four options. Which one actually survives our peak season and our old yard scanners?,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"- **Toshio**: @Kenji, survival is cheap. I care which one stops the yearly add-on bleed. Which one is a single, fixed bundle?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"- **Yumi**: @Toshio, a fixed bundle sounds safe, but if the scope shifts, who owns the mess? I need clear accountability.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, accountability is the trap. I’m looking for a system that doesn’t quietly age in place. Which one forces us to maintain it properly?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, maintenance is only half the battle. I need to know who actually trains the crews when the trainers leave.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Misaki"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Misaki: @Benjamin, maintenance is only half the battle. I need to know who actually trains the crews when the trainers leave.""}]}"
66,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: @Misaki, the on-site team at Anchor sounds promising for the yard, but I worry about the hardware mix.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, on-site presence doesn’t stop the invoice from climbing. I need a fixed configuration where the price is locked, not a modular trap.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, a fixed configuration is rigid. If our rules change again, who owns the rewrite? I need a partner who stays accountable, not just a locked price.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, rigidity is just another word for decay. If the configuration is fixed, we are just building a new dispatch tool to skip upgrades.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, rigidity is dangerous, but so is a partner who leaves us stranded. I need to know who actually stays to teach the crews when the initial rollout ends.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, the partner firm at Tessera handles training, but I worry they’ll vanish after the initial push. I need someone who stays for the long haul.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, staying is a cost. I need the price locked so the long tail doesn’t bleed us dry. Which option stops the yearly climb?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, locking the price doesn't lock the scope. If the rules change, a rigid system breaks. I need a partner who owns the rewrite, not just the invoice.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, you’re right that scope shifts break rigid systems. But a partner who leaves is worse. I need a system that forces us to maintain it, not one that rots in place.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I’m voting for Anchor. The on-site engineering team is the only option that guarantees someone stays to teach the crews, rather than leaving us stranded.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I’m voting for Anchor. The on-site team is the only one that can actually fix our yard hardware and survive the peak season without a freeze.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"I’m voting for Meridian. The fixed configuration locks the price, stopping the yearly add-on bleed that the invoices proved is our real enemy.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"I’m voting for Tessera. The partner firm handles the data lift and training, ensuring someone owns the mess when the scope shifts, unlike the unowned winter outage.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I’m voting for Meridian. A hosted suite with a regional team prevents the quiet aging of on-prem systems and keeps external work accountable, unlike the 2018 data lift.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
